/**

@page peano_main The generated main routine

\tableofcontents

The generated main is a small adapter between the generated solver repository
and exahype2::runner::Runner::launch(). The runner owns initialisation, the
phase order, the rank coordination, the reporting and the shutdown.

# Repository callbacks

The generated `SolverRepository` holds one instance of every solver of the
project. Its free functions forward every phase to every solver, and the main
collects them in an exahype2::runner::SolverRepositoryCallbacks record:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
result.allocate        = ::project::allocate;
result.initialise      = ::project::initialise;
result.performTimeStep = ::project::performTimeStep;
result.migrate         = ::project::migrate;
result.plot            = ::project::plot;
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The record also names the parameter loading, the help text, the memory
accounting, the refinement votes and the statistics getters of the solvers.

# Launch

The generated entry point has the following shape:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  ::exahype2::runner::RuntimeParameters::getInstance().setGeneratedDefaults(
    minimumTerminalTime,
    maximumTerminalTime,
    gridLevels,
    maximumGridLevels,
    projectName
  );

  return ::exahype2::runner::Runner::launch(
    DomainOffset,
    DomainSize,
    PeriodicBoundaries,
    createRepositoryCallbacks(),
    argc,
    argv
  );
}
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

`launch()` reads the runtime parameters, initialises tarch and Peano, builds
the grid, runs the phases and performs the matching shutdown sequence.

# SPMD control flow

Every rank runs the same phase. The global master decides the next step and
exahype2::runner::Runner::exchangeStep() distributes it with one allreduce, so
a phase has one collective order across the MPI ranks. Application code that
uses MPI or mesh data runs inside a solver phase and keeps that order.

# Python API

The Python API emits the solver classes, the solver repository, the runtime
parameters and the main routine from the project description. Application
code adds PDE terms, hooks and tracers to the solvers; there is no generated
step list to extend.

*/
